  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "gate.run_bounded enforces a wall-clock deadline (a sleeping Mac must not stretch the gate)",
  "spec": "Why: gate.py:47 uses proc.communicate(timeout=timeout_s), which counts monotonic time; on macOS that clock stops during sleep. On 2026-09-30 luna's T-0575 gate started 20:55, the Mac slept 21:10-22:21, and at 22:22 the gate had run 87 wall minutes with no timeout while the synchronous gate blocked every daemon stage (gotchas.md 2026-09-30).\nWhat: in _run, compute deadline = time.time() + timeout_s; loop proc.communicate(input on the first call only, timeout=min(30, max(0.1, deadline - time.time()))) catching TimeoutExpired until the process exits or time.time() >= deadline; on the deadline take the existing kill path (SIGTERM group, kill_grace_s, SIGKILL group, reap). Keep the return shape. Note communicate can only send input once: pass input on the first call and None after. Keep run_gate and running_gates unchanged.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused acceptance test in the foreground (uv run python -m pytest <id> -q). Never background a command and never run the full gate; the daemon gates externally. Acceptance ids are tests/<file>.py::<function or method name>; write the test as a unittest.TestCase method using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py::test_deadline_counts_wall_clock_sleep passes: with time.time patched to jump past the deadline while the child still runs, run_bounded returns timed_out True and the process group is gone, without waiting for timeout_s of monotonic time",
    "existing tests in tests/test_gate_timeout.py still pass; .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/gate.py",
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py"
